# The second story: not idle at all. Claude compacts its own context when a chunk of work is done.
title:   Claude can compact its own context when a piece of work is done
caption: Compaction can also happen while you are working. idle-compact gives Claude a tool that compacts the conversation right after its current reply. Use it when a piece of work is finished.
note:    This path skips both the 20-minute wait and the size check: it compacts one second after the reply ends, whatever the size.

# scene  <icon>  <hue>  <size from>-<size to>  <title> — <text>      sizes are percent of the graph's height
scene  cloud    blue    22-60   A long session — You and Claude work on a large task. The context grows.
scene  done     teal    60-86   A piece of work is finished — For example, the tests pass. Most of the history is no longer needed.
scene  ask      violet  86-88   Claude calls the tool — You ask for a compaction, or Claude decides to compact. Claude calls compact_after_turn.
scene  compact  green   88-10   Compaction after the reply — It runs one second after the reply ends. There is no 20-minute wait and no size check.
scene  back     green   10-24   The next task starts with a small context — The session continues. Each later message reads less.

graph    Context size — what every message has to carry
with     with idle-compact
without  without it: every later message reads the whole history

also     violet  Three tools for Claude — compact_after_turn compacts as soon as the current reply ends. config reads or changes the settings (how long to wait, how big is big enough) and takes effect at once. status shows the settings and what the timer is doing. Claude can use these to check and change idle-compact.

term  Tool — an action an add-on makes available to Claude. You do not call it yourself; you ask Claude in plain words and it uses the tool.
term  Turn — one round of the conversation: your message, and everything Claude does until its reply is done.
term  Context — everything Claude reads to answer you: the whole conversation so far, measured in tokens (a token is roughly three quarters of a word).
term  Compact — replace the conversation so far with a short summary of it and carry on from there. Details that are not in the summary are gone from Claude's view.
